member.summary:
A two-way link to one view model field, made with
UI.Bind(() => VM.Settings.Width). Controls read it and write it;
a write tells exactly that field's readers.

example.code:
public sealed class CounterViewModel : ViewModel
{
    public int Count;
    public Computed<bool> CanReset { get; }
    public Command Increment { get; }
    public Command Reset { get; }

    public CounterViewModel()
    {
        CanReset = Computed(() => Count > 0);
        Increment = Command(() => Count++);
        Reset = Command(() => Count = 0, canExecute: CanReset);
    }
}

member.remarks:
            What can be read:


fields and properties reached from a view model (become cells);

.Value of , , , and members of  (track themselves);

constants, captured locals, readonly fields, static readonly fields;

methods of the base library and math types, and methods or properties marked .

member.summary:
The first of its views whose ideal width fits the width offered, the last
one when none fits: a wide layout, then a narrow one. All are made at mount;
the ones not picked are hidden and run no updates.

example.code:
public sealed class CounterView : View<CounterViewModel>
{
    public CounterView(CounterViewModel vm) : base(vm) { }

    public override View Body =>
        VStack(spacing: 12,
            Text(() => VM.Count, format: "Count: {0}"),
            Button(Text("Reset"), () => VM.Reset));
}
